# fixture: trueup-draw-unfunded  (adversarial)
#
# a monthly tax true-up that the everyday accounts cannot pay. A 401(k)
# closed to a Roth books its whole balance as income that month, and the
# true-up sizes the month's tax from that income x12, so it asks for far
# more than the close withheld. The single-backstop draw takes the Wallet,
# spills to Checking, Checking clamps too, and the rest is reported
# unfunded. Only what the two accounts paid counts as withheld; booked in
# full, the annual true-up would refund the unpaid part in cash. Both
# everyday accounts are load-bearing. With Checking alone the named account
# supplies everything that is paid, so booking settled.supplied would look
# right; the second account is what separates "what the accounts paid" from
# both "what the first account paid" and "what was handed to the fallback".
# Having a fallback, it does not reach the draw with none; the conservation
# test's first plan does. The close goes to a Roth, not to Checking, so no
# deposit lands where the true-up draws. Every rate is zero and nothing runs
# after the close, so the year's refund is collected minus owed, by hand.
# tests/trueup-withholding-conservation.mjs holds the conservation law.

